# Desktop version bump

Whenever you change **desktop / extension** code in this repo (anything under
`src/ui`, `src/content`, `src/sites`, `src/background`, `src/interceptor`,
`src/lib` used by the overlay, etc.), bump `DESKTOP_VERSION` in
`src/desktopVersion.ts` in the **same** edit.

- Format: `0.1.N` — base `0.1`, third digit +1 each time (`0.1.0` → `0.1.1` → …
  `0.1.13`). Not git-based.
- That string is shown in the overlay header as `v0.1.13` and in
  `chrome://extensions` as `· d0.1.13`, so the user can confirm a reload picked
  up the change.
- Do **not** skip the bump on “tiny” fixes — the whole point is every prompt that
  changes code gets a new number.
- Phone / web (`src/web`) keeps using the existing git `build/version` stamp;
  only bump `DESKTOP_VERSION` for extension/desktop work.
